.TH SDL_iconv_utf8_locale 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_iconv_utf8_locale \- Convert a UTF-8 string to the current locale\(aqs character encoding.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_iconv_utf8_locale(S)    SDL_iconv_string(\(dq\(dq, \(dqUTF-8\(dq, S, SDL_strlen(S)+1)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a helper macro that might be more clear than calling
.BR SDL_iconv_string
directly\[char46] However, it double-evaluates its parameter, so do not use an expression with side-effects here\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I S
the string to convert\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a new string, converted to the new encoding, or NULL on error\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

